    {
      "id": "claim_f7ad54d0dc424f7492591221632400bf",
      "statement": "The setup's \"two claims travel in the token\" step adds latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp to the JWT's account-properties-claims through the auth feature's configuration: it reads the feature config with getFeatureConfig(srvId, 'auth') and writes it back with updateFeatureConfig(srvId, 'auth'), appending to any existing claims. There is no separate /auth-config endpoint. The Guards rule condition reads @user.latestConsents.tos and @user.latestConsents.pp from the token claims, not the database, so the gate works without a database round-trip per request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L135-L161",
